                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I am going to make the argument that you need this game in your life. Prepare yourself for my evidence:\n\n1. Your hands are planet-destroying dragons. In the early days of gaming, that would have been argument enough, but these days, gamers are a grim and experienced bunch. You need more. I understand. \n\n2. If you are like me, i.e. uneasy with movement in VR, this game somehow lets you whip around the damn galaxy at warp speeds eating planets and it doesn't feel, you know, barfy. It's feels GREAT. And that brings me to:\n\n3. Movement. Man, it's so good. Intuitive as hell. Five minutes after you start, you'll be streaming through the stars, burning planets to dust, freeing massive spacefish from space prisons, dodging lasers, and it just feels SMOOOOTH. Plus:\n\n4. Dragon Hyperspace. It's rad. \n\n5. Also, bosses. They're huge, spooky, and pretty as hell.\n\n6. SPEAKING OF PRETTY, the health bar thing is cool. You should see it. I won't spoil it\n\n7. Last and most important, you can make the dragons smooch.\n\nIn summary, you should get this game if:\n\n* You've ever wanted to be a dragon. \n* You've ever wanted to fly. \n* You've ever wanted to be in space. \n* You hate planets and space fortresses.\n* You like freeing giant space monsters.\n* You like games.\n\nThank you.",
